    }
  ],
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "No direct ascorbic acid oral bioavailability record is present in the supplied cards.",
    "Dose dependence of ascorbic acid absorption is not captured; at very high doses F may approach or fall below 20%.",
    "Active transport (e.g., SVCT1/2) contribution is inferred from the query prior caveat, not from a measured record.",
    "Transfer from glucose/mannitol/sorbitol contexts is qualitative; species, patient status, and doses differ."
  ],
  "decision_summary": "Predicted high (F ≥ 20%): transferable sugar/polyol contexts (glucose, mannitol, sorbitol) show oral bioavailability at or above 20% despite low passive permeability, and the low physicochemical prior is not affirmative evidence for F < 20%; gemcitabine's low F is mechanism-specific and does not transfer."
}

